<title>USA: Sequana Therapeutics completes acquisition.</title>
<headline>Sequana Therapeutics completes acquisition.</headline>
<dateline>LA JOLLA, Calif. 1996-10-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Sequana Therapeutics Inc said Wednesday it has completed its previously announced acquisition of NemaPharm Inc, a developer of drug discovery technologies using the nematode worm, C. elegans.</p>
<p>Final financial terms were undisclosed.</p>
<p>Using NemaPharm's NemaScreen technology, Sequana plans to develop novel high-throughput screens for therapeutic leads.</p>
<p>&quot;Already, the company has provided us with useful functional information to complement our research activities, particularly in the area of human obesity,&quot; Tim Harris, senior chief technical officer, said in a statement.</p>
</text>
